## 🛡️ Compatibility Assessment

### REST Breaking Changes

None detected.

### Downstream Breaking Changes

<a id="finding-pr-43308-lro-recognition"></a>
### Three generated SDK methods change from basic to long-running

- **Severity:** high
- **Confidence:** high
- **Summary:** The wire contract is unchanged, but ScenarioConfigurations.execute, legacy ScenarioConfigurations.cancel, and ScenarioRuns.cancel now expose poller/LRO return types and asynchronous completion semantics.
- **Evidence:** Before the change, generated clients treat the three methods as ordinary operations rather than long-running operations.; After the change, generated clients expose Location-polled LRO behavior with typed final responses.; Base/head OpenAPI method, path, parameters, responses, x-ms-long-running-operation, and final-state-via values are identical.
- **TypeSpec source:** [lro-helpers.tsp:L22-L119](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/a3b8933eb6ce030faa6abc6d354fc97e30f02e96/specification/chaos/resource-manager/Microsoft.Chaos/Chaos/lro-helpers.tsp#L22-L119), [scenarioConfiguration.tsp:L48-L84](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/a3b8933eb6ce030faa6abc6d354fc97e30f02e96/specification/chaos/resource-manager/Microsoft.Chaos/Chaos/scenarioConfiguration.tsp#L48-L84), [scenarioRun.tsp:L44-L52](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/a3b8933eb6ce030faa6abc6d354fc97e30f02e96/specification/chaos/resource-manager/Microsoft.Chaos/Chaos/scenarioRun.tsp#L44-L52)


